libfs Changes
===============


Unreleased
----------
* FIX: `write_nifti()` no longer emits an identity quaternion in the qform.  The unit quaternion is now computed from the rotation part of the MGH `Mdc` matrix (with reflections encoded via a negative `pixdim[0]`), keeping qform consistent with sform.

v0.6.0 -- Improved generic mesh file readers
----------------------------------------------
* NEW: Add new features to OBJ reader (quads, relative indices, texture coords, ...) and improve its security
* NEW: Improve security of the OFF and PLY readers
* NEW: Add `preserve_vertex_indices` flag to `Mesh::from_obj()` to load OBJ files without vertex expansion (see note below)

Note that loading texture coordinates from OBJ files and saving them as per-vertex properties requires vertex expansion, as these are stored in the file for each face edge, and one vertex will occur listed several times, as it is part of several face edges. This means that after loading, the mesh will have more vertices than listed in the source mesh file, as typical in computer graphics applications. This ONLY affects meshes with texture coords. All other meshes are still guaranteed to have the vertex listed at position N in the file to be at the respective vertex index in the loaded mesh. To load an OBJ file without vertex expansion (e.g. to keep FreeSurfer-style per-vertex indexing, so the vertex at position N in the file stays at index N in the mesh), pass `preserve_vertex_indices=true` to `Mesh::from_obj()`. In this mode texture coordinates and vertex normals are ignored and not loaded, and the mesh keeps the vertices exactly as listed in the file.


v0.5.0 -- NIfTI support and bug fixes
--------------------------------------
* BRK: remove previously deprecated version defined with typos like LIBFS_VERISION_MAJOR, use LIBFS_VERSION_MAJOR etc instead
* FIX: copy-paste bug in `Mesh::from_obj()` — face vertex index 3 (v2) incorrectly used v0raw instead of v2raw when stripping slash-suffix texture/normal indices from OBJ files.
* FIX: uninitialized memory read (UB) in `_fread3()` — the 4th byte of the uint32_t was uninitialized before being passed through the endian swap.
* FIX: `Mesh::construct_grid()` did not reset the y-coordinate (`cur_y`) between grid rows, producing distorted geometry.
* FIX: reversed face winding in `Mesh::construct_cube()` — 3 of 6 cube faces (left, top, back) had normals pointing inward instead of outward.
* FIX: reversed face winding in `Mesh::construct_pyramid()` — the 2 base triangles had normals pointing +Z (up into the pyramid) instead of -Z (down/outward).
* FIX: missing bounds check in `write_mgh()` — Mdc and Pxyz_c vectors are now validated before indexed access when ras_good_flag == 1.
* FIX: weak hash function for `edge_set` — replaced symmetric XOR-only hash with a proper hash combine to reduce collisions.
* FIX: dead endian-swap code in `_fwritei3()` — removed no-op byte-swapping of individual unsigned chars (extracted bytes are already in correct order).
* NEW: the `Mesh` struct now has a `vertex_colors` field (std::vector<uint8_t>, 3-per-vertex interleaved RGB, empty if no colors) for storing vertex colors read from mesh files.
* NEW: `Mesh::from_ply()` now parses vertex colors (property uchar red/green/blue) when present in the PLY header.
* NEW: `Mesh::from_off()` now parses vertex colors when the file uses COFF format (color OFF).
* NEW: `Mesh::from_obj()` now parses per-vertex colors from OBJ files using the widely-supported `x y z r g b` convention (6 floats per vertex line, where the last 3 are RGB as floats in [0,1]).
* NEW: `Mesh::to_obj(col)` / `Mesh::to_obj_file(f, col)` overloads — export OBJ files with vertex colors using the same `x y z r g b` convention.
* NEW: `fs::write_mesh(mesh, filename, col)` overload — write a mesh to PLY, OBJ, or OFF format with vertex colors, auto-detected by file extension.
* NEW: Add support for writing annot files
* NEW: Add support for reading and writing NIfTI v1 format, including files with FreeSurfer hack


v0.4.2: Fix version defines
-----------------------------
* FIX: fix typo in version defines, e.g., `LIBFS_VERISION_MAJOR 0` => fixed to `LIBFS_VERSION_MAJOR 0`. The old ones remain for now as well but are deprecated, use the correct ones with correct spelling.
* DEV: Improve developer docs by adding a new section on making a release


v0.4.1: Security and Integration
--------------------------------
* Make the libfs version available as integers for easier compile time checks in client apps by defining integers LIBFS_VERSION_MAJOR, LIBFS_VERSION_MINOR, and LIBFS_VERSION_PATCH in addition to the string LIBFS_VERSION.
* Add new INTERFACE cmake target for easier integration
* Add various security checks when reading files, to prevent malformed headers / files from causing issues


v0.4.0: Colormap support for per-vertex data
--------------------------------------------
* Add new static utility function `fs::util::viridis` that maps per-vertex numeric data (e.g. the output of `fs::read_curv_data` or `fs::read_desc_data`) to RGB colors using the Viridis perceptually-uniform colormap. The returned `std::vector<uint8_t>` is in the exact interleave format (3 bytes per vertex: red, green, blue) expected by the mesh exporters `fs::Mesh::to_ply` / `fs::Mesh::to_ply_file` (and the OFF variants), so it closes the gap between reading morphometry data and exporting a colored brain mesh. The colormap is implemented from its official 256-sample lookup table (the same data used by matplotlib) with linear interpolation between samples, so there are no external dependencies. The data range is auto-normalized from the finite (non-NaN) min/max of the input by default, and can be overridden via optional `vmin` / `vmax` parameters. NaN values in the input are mapped to a configurable color via the new `nan_r` / `nan_g` / `nan_b` parameters, which defaults to white (255, 255, 255) following the standard convention in neuroimaging where missing data (e.g. the medial wall) is shown in white.
* Add new example program `examples/vertex_color_export/vertex_color_export.cpp` that demonstrates the full pipeline: it reads a brain hemisphere mesh (`lh.white`), per-vertex cortical thickness data (`lh.thickness`), and a cortex label (`lh.cortex.label`), masks the medial wall vertices (those outside the cortex label) to NaN, maps the thickness to vertex colors with `fs::util::viridis` (NaN -> white), and exports the colored mesh to a PLY file.


v0.3.4: Windows and MSVC support
--------------------------------
* Fix incorrect reading of binary data under Windows/MSVC, run unit tests under Windows on CI system.
* Fix lots of minor warnings on higher WARN levels during compilation (implicit size_t <-> int32_t casts).


v0.3.3: Submesh support
-----------------------
* Add function libfs::Mesh::submesh_vertex to create a submesh based on given vertex indices.
* Add static function libfs::Mesh::curv_data_for_orig_mesh to map per-vertex data for a submesh back to the full, original mesh.v0.3.3: Submeshes


v0.3.2: Version information
---------------------------
* Add a define LIBFS_VERISION, which makes the version available.


v0.3.1: Logging and smoothing of per-vertex data
-------------------------------------------------
* Add `fs::Mesh::construct_grid` function to construct 2D grids.
* Add `fs::Mesh::construct_pyramid` function.
* Add option to control logging via log levels. See API docs main page for usage info.
* Add support for smoothing per-vertex data on meshes, see new function `fs::Mesh::smooth_pvd_nn`.
* Related to `fs::Mesh::smooth_pvd_nn`, add new mesh functions `fs::Mesh::as_adjlist`, `fs::Mesh::as_matrix`, and `fs::Mesh::as_edgeset`.


v0.3.0: Fully documented
-------------------------
* Finish API documentation: all members and functions documented, many with example usage in the doc string.
* Add support for writing FreeSurfer brain meshes in surf format, see function `fs::write_surf`.
* Add support for constructing basic meshes, see `fs::Mesh::construct_cube`. Mainly for examples.
* Add general wrapper function for writing meshes in different formats, auto-detected from file extension, see `fs::write_mesh`.
* BREAKING: Remove duplicate `fs::fullpath` function. Use `fs::util::fullpath` instead.


v0.2.2: Exceptions for the world
---------------------------------
* Add `fs::read_subjectsfile` function.
* Throw exceptions in all places where `exit` was still being called. Document potentially thrown exceptions in function doc strings.
* Fix mesh indexing bug.


v0.2.1: Annot support and much better docs
-------------------------------------------
* Finish rough first version of API documentation.
* Add structs `Annot` and `Colortable` with many convenience member functions that model brain parcellations.
* Add support for reading brain surface parcellations from annot files, see `fs::read_annot` function.
* Add example for reading annot files.


 v0.2.0 Streaming and MGZ support
----------------------------------
* BREAKING: change order of arguments for all functions reading streams.
* BREAKING: rename all `sread_` functions to `read_` and use overloading.
* Add stream-based versions for reading various formats, including MGH. This allows for MGZ support, see `examples/read_mgz/`.
* Add many new member functions to structs and use them throughout the library.
* Add Curv struct and new `fs::read_curv` function that reads into it.
* BREAKING: rename old `fs::read_curv` function that reads only the data part to `fs::read_curv_data`.


 v0.1: Initial release
-----------------------
* Read and write FreeSurfer per-vertex data from and to binary curv format files (like `$SUBJECTS_DIR/surf/lh.thickness`), see `fs::read_curv` function.
* Read FreeSurfer brain surface meshes from binary surf format files (like `$SUBJECTS_DIR/surf/lh.white`), see `fs::read_surf` function.
* Read FreeSurfer ASCII label files (like `$SUBJECTS_DIR/label/lh.cortex.label`), see `fs::read_label` function.
* Read and write FreeSurfer 4D volume files (typically 3D voxels + a fourth time/subject dimension) from binary MGH format files (like `$SUBJECTS_DIR/mri/brain.mgh or $SUBJECTS_DIR/surf/lh.thickness.fwhm5.fsaverage.mgh`).

